{"name":"Dead Sea Scrolls","language":"aramaic","source":"A. Lukaszewski, "Chrestomathy" in "The Value of Qumran Aramaic for Addressing the New Testament Aramaic Problem" (Ph.D. diss., University of Saint Andrews, 2004). Used by permission. See also J. T. Milik, with the collaboration of M. Black, The Books of Enoch: Aramaic Fragments of Qumran Cave 4 (Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1976). (For a list of disagreements between Lukaszewski and Milik, see the "Disagreements" section below.)","data":{"EN1-1":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q201","source":"4Q201"},"EN1-2":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q202","source":"4Q202"},"EN1-3":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q204","source":"4Q204"},"EN1-4":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q205","source":"4Q205"},"EN1-5":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q206","source":"4Q206"},"EN1-6":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q207","source":"4Q207"},"EN1-7":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q208","source":"4Q208"},"EN1-8":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q209","source":"4Q209"},"EN1-9":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q210","source":"4Q210"},"EN1-10":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q211","source":"4Q211"},"EN1-11":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q212","source":"4Q212"},"EN1-12":{"name":"Enoch Fragment 4Q247","source":"4Q247"}}}